              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "In *The Vampire Diaries*, Elena Gilbert turns into a vampire across two key episodes at the turn of Season 3 and Season 4:\n\n### 1. The Death & Transition \u2014 Season 3, Episode 22 (\"The Departed\")\nElena technically dies with vampire blood in her system in the Season 3 finale. \n* **How it happens:** Earlier in the episode, Dr. Meredith Fell secretly treats Elena\u2019s severe brain hemorrhage with Damon Salvatore's vampire blood. Later, while riding in a truck with Matt Donovan, Rebekah Mikaelson forces them off Wickery Bridge and into the water. \n* Stefan Salvatore arrives to rescue them, but Elena insists he save Matt first. By the time Stefan returns for Elena, she has drowned. Because she died with Damon's blood in her system, the episode ends with Elena suddenly waking up on a slab in the morgue, starting her transition into a vampire.\n\n### 2. Completing the Transition \u2014 Season 4, Episode 1 (\"Growing Pains\")\nElena officially becomes a vampire in the Season 4 premiere.\n* **How it happens:** Elena wakes up in transition and struggles with the choice of whether to feed on human blood to complete the process or let herself die. \n* After being captured and locked up by the town's Founder's Council, she begins dying from the transition. With Stefan's help, she is finally able to feed on human blood (specifically from a guard), completing her transformation and officially becoming a vampire.",
